SELECT (SELECT id FROM public.job_sources WHERE key = 'remoteok'),
  'seed-011',
  (SELECT id FROM public.companies WHERE slug = 'gitlab'),
  'GitLab', 'Fullstack JavaScript Developer Staff', 'fullstack javascript developer staff',
  (SELECT id FROM public.career_tracks WHERE key = 'fullstack'),
  (SELECT rv.id FROM public.track_role_variants rv JOIN public.career_tracks ct ON ct.id = rv.track_id WHERE ct.key = 'fullstack' AND rv.key = 'fullstack_js'),
  'staff',
  'Remote',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  true, 'global', 'remoto_global', 'en', 'full-time',
  'About the role
GitLab is hiring a Staff Fullstack JavaScript Developer to join a distributed, remote-first engineering team. You will help us scale our product across the stack.

What you will do
- Design, build and operate reliable systems in production.
- Partner with product and design to ship user-facing value continuously.
- Improve testing, observability and developer experience.
- Mentor peers and take part in technical decisions.

Requirements
- Solid hands-on experience with PostgreSQL.
- Solid hands-on experience with MySQL.
- Solid hands-on experience with Testes Automatizados.
- Solid hands-on experience with Playwright.
- Solid hands-on experience with Next.js.
- Solid hands-on experience with Express.js.

Nice to have
- Familiarity with Vitest.
- Familiarity with Python.
- Familiarity with Spring Boot.

Benefits
- Fully remote, flexible hours, home office stipend, learning budget and paid time off.',
  150500, 187400, 'USD', 'year', false,
  'https://jobs.example.com/gitlab/seed-011',
  now() - interval '44 days', now() + interval '56 days',
  md5('gitlab|Fullstack JavaScript Developer Staff|remoto_global'), true
